1
00:00:00,260 --> 00:00:02,020
(Churan reacts to EP1)

2
00:00:02,880 --> 00:00:04,920
Churan, did you watch the first episode?

3
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:07,400
I did.

4
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:08,480
(What's with that reaction?)

5
00:00:08,480 --> 00:00:09,840
So, how do you think you did?

6
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:11,720
(Speechless)
I was honestly speechless.

7
00:00:13,160 --> 00:00:14,600
I didn't realize

8
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:15,640
I looked that clueless.

9
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:16,560
Were you clueless?

10
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:17,480
(Haven't watched it yet)
I haven't watched it.

11
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:19,220
(Cracking herself up)

12
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:21,360
(Jogging his memory)
You said there were four characters.

13
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:24,160
I was...

14
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:26,640
(What a first!)
I was speechless. Goodness!

15
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:27,920
(Now he's intrigued)
What happened?

16
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:29,240
(Dying to know)
Give me the details.

17
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:30,880
I acted out five characters for her.

18
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:32,759
I showed her right from the start.

19
00:00:32,759 --> 00:00:34,920
And Churan just kept nodding,

20
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:35,800
telling me to keep going.

21
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:37,520
Then when it was time to pass it on,

22
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:38,720
I asked her
how many characters there were.

23
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:40,240
Churan said four.

24
00:00:41,880 --> 00:00:42,920
Four or five, maybe.

25
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:47,160
She even voted Hu out.

26
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:47,800
And she was still saying

27
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:48,960
she thought it was Hu.

28
00:00:50,220 --> 00:00:51,260
(Poor me...)

29
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:53,160
Hu was so furious.

30
00:00:53,820 --> 00:00:55,300
(Too embarrassed)

31
00:00:55,820 --> 00:00:58,300
(The Natural High crew lines up)

32
00:00:58,740 --> 00:01:00,640
(Getting into position)

33
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:02,000
Like this, right?

34
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:02,800
Like this?

35
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:04,280
That's just like Ma Li's pose.

36
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:05,360
Does it look like Ma Li?

37
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:07,880
Really?

38
00:01:07,880 --> 00:01:09,920
(Godspeed)
Remember our movie Godspeed?

39
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:10,680
That one scene...

40
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:11,720
Which way do we face?

41
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:13,000
This way. For sure.

42
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:13,800
In one row?

43
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:15,400
Or like this in one row?

44
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:19,920
How about we stand like this?

45
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:20,440
Like this, in one straight row.

46
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:21,320
(Standing side by side)
Sure.

47
00:01:21,940 --> 00:01:22,940
(Getting Anyu into position first)

48
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:24,360
Let's pose him, too.

49
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:26,960
Then we have to face his way.

50
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:29,400
Like this?

51
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:30,960
Left hand?

52
00:01:32,480 --> 00:01:33,440
No, the other way.

53
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:35,980
(Getting in sync)

54
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:36,680
Let's do it.

55
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:37,400
Come on.

56
00:01:37,720 --> 00:01:39,280
- Natural High!
- Natural High!

57
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:45,160
These three trees are pretty cool.

58
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:46,880
They're actually really nice.

59
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:49,520
(Let me see)
Three trees next to five pines.

60
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:51,840
(Photo time)
Three, two, one.

61
00:01:53,640 --> 00:01:55,200
Some people say they can't do this.

62
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:56,080
Can you guys do it?

63
00:01:56,360 --> 00:01:57,040
That's easy.

64
00:01:57,040 --> 00:01:57,680
Mine won't spread.

65
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:00,960
I'm cramping up.

66
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:01,680
See? I can spread them.

67
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:02,760
But this one sticks up.

68
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:04,360
See? It pops up when I relax.

69
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:06,480
(The calluses say it all)
Whoa, these are some serious calluses.

70
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:07,600
Training a lot lately, huh?

71
00:02:08,340 --> 00:02:10,580
(Teng's got jokes and sauce tips)

72
00:02:11,039 --> 00:02:12,400
Don't we have chili oil?

73
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:13,280
It's on the table.

74
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:14,240
On the table?

75
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:14,760
Yeah, right there.

76
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:15,680
Chili oil.

77
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:16,720
(Chili oil is a must)
Can't go without chili oil.

78
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:17,480
What's all this?

79
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:20,080
(Flavor overload)
This dipping sauce is amazing.

80
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:21,040
(So much flavor)
So good.

81
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:21,480
Dip what?

82
00:02:21,480 --> 00:02:21,960
It's really good.

83
00:02:21,960 --> 00:02:22,520
The meat.

84
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:23,960
Dip the meat or the glass noodles.

85
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:24,600
It's all delicious.

86
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:25,480
Even the noodles with pickled cabbage.

87
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:27,440
Should we throw in some cilantro
or anything?

88
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:27,960
(Knows his food)
Nope, nothing.

89
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:29,720
(Knows his food)
Those two are plenty flavorful.

90
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:33,200
Have you guys ever tried...

91
00:02:33,760 --> 00:02:35,280
What's that Hebei specialty called?

92
00:02:35,640 --> 00:02:36,280
Sheep intestines?
[*Yang chang: maximize strengths]

93
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:39,560
("Bi duan"?)
[*Bi duan: Avoid weaknesses]

94
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:40,600
Have you both tried "bi duan"?

95
00:02:40,860 --> 00:02:41,740
(Got the joke instantly)

96
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:42,680
What are you talking about?

97
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:43,420
Ever tried "bi duan"?
[*From the Chinese idiom]

98
00:02:43,420 --> 00:02:44,560
Ever tried "bi duan"?
["Maximize strengths and avoid weaknesses"]

99
00:02:44,940 --> 00:02:46,360
(Trying to figure it out...)

100
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:47,400
Well? Have you tried it or not?

101
00:02:48,180 --> 00:02:49,800
(Messing with Chengcheng)

102
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:50,280
Teng is asking you.

103
00:02:50,280 --> 00:02:50,800
Have you tried it or not?

104
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:52,940
(That knowing smile)

105
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:53,520
(Completely lost)
What's that?

106
00:02:53,540 --> 00:02:54,260
"Bi duan".
[*Avoid weaknesses]

107
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:55,640
(Interpreter to the rescue)
Play to your strengths, avoid weaknesses.

108
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:57,520
I thought it was some kind of...

109
00:02:58,720 --> 00:02:59,400
"Bi duan".
[*Avoid weaknesses]

110
00:03:00,220 --> 00:03:02,260
(It was a pun all along)

111
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:05,060
(Teng's love language?
Chewy, chewy tendon!)

112
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:06,600
(Remembering that lamb tendon)

113
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:07,880
Teng took me to try it
for the first time.

114
00:03:07,880 --> 00:03:10,080
(A whole new experience)
I'd never had it growing up.

115
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:10,680
That was my first time.

116
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:11,680
Good stuff, right?

117
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:12,000
Yeah.

118
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:13,720
You said you had strong teeth,

119
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:14,400
and I didn't buy it.

120
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:16,920
Now I know you weren't kidding.

121
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:17,400
(Proud of himself)
Yep.

122
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:19,480
That tendon was like...

123
00:03:19,480 --> 00:03:20,960
(Crazy springy)
a trampoline spring.

124
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:21,160
Yeah.

125
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:22,760
It's not like the tendon we usually eat.

126
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:24,280
That's beef tendon.

127
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:26,000
This was grilled lamb tendon.

128
00:03:26,320 --> 00:03:27,760
No boiling. Straight on the grill.

129
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:29,160
Straight on the grill?

130
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:31,680
Yeah. Usually, your jaw hurts here.

131
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:33,160
But that stuff? It hurts up here.

132
00:03:33,760 --> 00:03:35,080
Right up to your temples.

133
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:36,360
And he just kept chewing,

134
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:37,800
(Chew, chew, chew)
like it was nothing.

135
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:38,680
After that meal,

136
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:40,400
Bai was rubbing his temples next to me.

137
00:03:40,460 --> 00:03:42,000
(Jaw muscles begging for mercy)

138
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,080
(Looks like eye exercises)
You'd think his eyes were tired.

139
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:46,240
Like he was doing eye exercises.

140
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:47,400
Seriously, that tendon...

141
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:49,480
And Teng was so generous.

142
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:50,960
(What a good buddy)
He ordered a ton of skewers.

143
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:54,040
It was my first time eating with him.

144
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:55,000
I couldn't just say no.

145
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,400
So poor Bai just sat there,

146
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:58,920
rubbing his head.

147
00:03:59,880 --> 00:04:01,760
The more you ate,
the more he thought you liked it.

148
00:04:01,760 --> 00:04:02,560
So he kept ordering.

149
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:04,760
Yeah, and I barely had any.

150
00:04:05,940 --> 00:04:08,580
(Chatting before the game)

151
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,480
We should've come on motorcycles.

152
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:12,680
(Now he's excited)
Let's ride back.

153
00:04:13,640 --> 00:04:14,640
It'd be freezing on the ride back.

154
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:15,640
We'd have snot

155
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:16,880
flying behind us.

156
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:18,120
(Can totally picture it)
You'd be riding up front,

157
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:19,320
(Can totally picture it)
with snot flying out behind you.

158
00:04:19,839 --> 00:04:21,320
I went riding with them last year.

159
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:22,160
They had Harleys,

160
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:23,160
and I had a rally bike.

161
00:04:23,840 --> 00:04:25,840
They kept getting up while riding.

162
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:26,920
So I asked why they kept popping up

163
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:28,560
like rally riders.

164
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:29,480
(Curious)
Turns out,

165
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:31,440
their heated seats
were burning their butts.

166
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:32,440
Meanwhile, I was freezing.

167
00:04:32,920 --> 00:04:34,360
My hands were frozen stiff.

168
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:35,880
(The difference between bikes)

169
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:38,200
Everybody, stand up.

170
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:40,280
Head to the starting line.

171
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,500
(Gets up)

172
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:48,280
What's that?

173
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:53,400
Wait, there's glass?

174
00:04:58,200 --> 00:04:59,320
That glass is spotless.

175
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:00,280
Right? I thought...

176
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:01,360
Even Churan didn't see the glass.

177
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:02,320
(Same here)
I didn't see it either.

178
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:03,560
Seriously?

179
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:06,600
I was wondering
why that ring wasn't swaying.

180
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:08,080
I thought it was hanging from above.

181
00:05:08,140 --> 00:05:10,580
(Guess I'm too clean)

182
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:14,160
How else would that ring float there?

183
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:16,560
(He's got his own logic)
I thought it was hanging by a wire.

184
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:17,680
Teng, with eyesight like that,

185
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:19,280
it's no wonder you can't see a thing.

186
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:20,600
Please stop riding motorcycles.

187
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:21,280
Seriously.

188
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:23,000
Please don't ride anymore.

189
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,740
(Your concern is duly noted)

190
00:05:25,020 --> 00:05:27,740
(Bai strikes with another random joke)

191
00:05:31,260 --> 00:05:32,460
(Leaning way back)

192
00:05:35,740 --> 00:05:36,860
(Bing caught that)

193
00:05:36,860 --> 00:05:37,120
(Witness +1)

194
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:38,080
(Witness +1)
What's with that reaction?

195
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:40,920
Jingting's got such a deadpan style.

196
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:46,240
Back in Shanghai, we'd call

197
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:47,720
that deadpan humor.

198
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:49,040
Deadpan what?

199
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:50,080
Deadpan...

200
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:51,200
Humor.

201
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:51,920
It means...

202
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:53,560
Funny.

203
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:55,400
Like a joke or a punch line.

204
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:58,840
You barely crack a smile, and...

205
00:05:58,840 --> 00:05:59,680
Keep a straight face.

206
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:00,680
That's deadpan humor.

207
00:06:00,820 --> 00:06:02,280
(Bai, the king of deadpan)

208
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:03,600
(Bai, the king of deadpan)
Just vote me out.

209
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:08,320
Bai!

210
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:10,760
(Where'd he go?)
Bai's not coming back.

211
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:12,480
Beijing's northernmost.

212
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:18,440
(Promoting his hometown)
Welcome to my beautiful hometown,

213
00:06:18,440 --> 00:06:19,400
(Promoting his hometown)
Huairou.

214
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:23,360
That's Huairou hospitality for you.

215
00:06:23,740 --> 00:06:26,340
(Churan's instincts are on point today)

216
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:28,280
No, this is how Churan thinks.

217
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:29,400
(She's been figured out)
If you don't suspect her,

218
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:29,960
you're innocent.

219
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:32,160
But if you suspect her,

220
00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:33,120
you're guilty.

221
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:34,040
(She's been exposed)

222
00:06:34,040 --> 00:06:35,240
Am I wrong?

223
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:36,600
Not today, though.

224
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:38,200
Today, I just had this...

225
00:06:38,200 --> 00:06:38,840
weird feeling...

226
00:06:38,840 --> 00:06:39,760
(Trusting her sixth sense)

227
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:40,760
telling me something.

228
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:41,680
A gut feeling.

229
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:42,960
Intuition.

230
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:44,360
Did Huairou guide you?

231
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:45,720
I just had a feeling.

232
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:46,640
What kind of feeling?

233
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:48,400
My sixth sense today

234
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:49,560
was actually pretty spot-on.

235
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:51,760
Then why'd you ignore it?

236
00:06:51,760 --> 00:06:52,520
I just didn't stick with my picks.

237
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:55,520
(Teng backs her up)
Your instincts were spot-on today.

238
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:56,480
Right?

239
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:58,440
But when it came time to choose,

240
00:06:58,440 --> 00:07:00,880
everyone else's reactions threw me off.

241
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:01,840
(For example...)
Like what?

242
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:04,320
Like in the first round...

243
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:06,560
Wait, who did we pick again?

244
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:09,440
By the end of this episode,

245
00:07:09,440 --> 00:07:10,400
will you even remember us?

246
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:15,520
(Memory overload)
We've voted out so many people today.

247
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:17,160
That happened a few hours...

248
00:07:17,960 --> 00:07:19,520
Like three hours ago, right?

249
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:20,480
Let me think.

250
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:22,640
We picked Teng

251
00:07:22,640 --> 00:07:24,720
in the first round, right?

252
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:26,400
No, it was Hu.

253
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:27,860
(Sorry, I mixed it up)

254
00:07:28,260 --> 00:07:30,880
(Time for Dr. Chen's science lesson)

255
00:07:30,880 --> 00:07:31,920
Our next game

256
00:07:31,920 --> 00:07:34,040
starts with a little science lesson.

257
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:35,400
Let's welcome Dr. Chen.

258
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:38,520
Dr. Chen.

259
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:39,360
This round,

260
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:40,480
I've got an animal to introduce.

261
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:41,760
Every October,

262
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:42,800
a mysterious creature

263
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:44,240
flies south to Beijing.

264
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:45,480
People from all over the city

265
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:47,200
come out to catch a glimpse of this...

266
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:48,120
cat.

267
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:49,080
What kind of cat?

268
00:07:49,080 --> 00:07:50,000
A cat?

269
00:07:50,520 --> 00:07:51,760
People love spotting them,

270
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:53,440
especially in the parks.

271
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:55,200
They go looking every evening.

272
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:57,920
Turns out, it's an owl

273
00:07:57,920 --> 00:07:59,440
called the long-eared owl.

274
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:02,040
(Footage from online)
Every year, these owls

275
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:03,800
spend their summers up north.

276
00:08:04,240 --> 00:08:06,240
They reach Beijing in October.

277
00:08:06,240 --> 00:08:08,040
And they've got a superpower.

278
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:11,480
Even in pitch-black darkness,

279
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:15,200
they can locate prey by sound alone.

280
00:08:15,580 --> 00:08:17,040
(Oh, I see)

281
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:19,000
When it's completely dark,

282
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:21,400
they can hear the tiniest sounds.

283
00:08:24,140 --> 00:08:25,460
(Learned something new)

284
00:08:26,260 --> 00:08:28,460
(Funny moments from the car ride)

285
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:30,440
You're pretty nearsighted, right?

286
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:31,160
My prescription is minus seven.

287
00:08:31,540 --> 00:08:32,120
(Whoa!)

288
00:08:32,120 --> 00:08:34,080
(Curious Bai strikes again)
Are your contacts thicker than ours?

289
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:35,120
No, same thickness.

290
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:36,600
I think all contacts are pretty similar.

291
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:37,760
My glasses are really thick, though.

292
00:08:38,460 --> 00:08:39,760
(Good to know)

293
00:08:39,760 --> 00:08:41,600
How'd your eyesight get so bad?

294
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:45,120
I spent too much time
on the computer as a kid.

295
00:08:46,640 --> 00:08:47,720
Not reading the news, I bet.

296
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:48,440
(Since you asked...)
What games did you play?

297
00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:48,880
Yeah.

298
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:49,920
(Staring)

299
00:08:49,920 --> 00:08:51,000
And I worked through

300
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:52,680
the Five-Three study guides

301
00:08:52,880 --> 00:08:53,520
(Such a model student)
every single day.

302
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:55,360
What's that got to do with computers?

303
00:08:55,520 --> 00:08:56,520
That's studying.

304
00:08:56,800 --> 00:08:58,080
Is that your fake persona, Churan?

305
00:08:58,800 --> 00:08:59,440
Are we filming?

306
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:01,120
Make sure you get all that.

307
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:01,940
(Just teasing)

308
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:03,600
I'm starving.

309
00:09:04,400 --> 00:09:04,920
Already?

310
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:07,680
I ate a ton of nuts this afternoon.

311
00:09:07,680 --> 00:09:08,365
Nuts?

312
00:09:11,040 --> 00:09:13,320
Don't even get me started on those nuts.

313
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:14,600
After I was eliminated
in the first round,

314
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:16,520
I couldn't stop eating them.

315
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:21,400
(Couldn't resist)
My mouth was sore from all that chewing.

316
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:22,080
The shells were piled sky-high.

317
00:09:24,280 --> 00:09:25,080
I ate way too much.

318
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:26,680
I'm not touching them tomorrow.

319
00:09:26,880 --> 00:09:28,040
(We heard that)
We got that on camera.

320
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:31,440
I swear, tomorrow I'm not eating

321
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:33,240
a single thing from that nut platter.

322
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:35,920
There's our transition shot
for tomorrow.

323
00:09:35,920 --> 00:09:37,160
Cut to you eating nuts again.

324
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:38,400
Fruit doesn't count.

325
00:09:38,400 --> 00:09:39,260
(Already making exceptions)

326
00:09:39,640 --> 00:09:40,680
Already making excuses.

327
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:42,640
No, I need my vitamins.

328
00:09:42,640 --> 00:09:44,960
You need healthy fats and nutrients too.

329
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:46,440
I've got enough fat already.

330
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:48,000
You've slimmed down a lot lately.

331
00:09:48,860 --> 00:09:49,840
(Feeling motivated)

332
00:09:49,840 --> 00:09:50,240
Bai,

333
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:52,560
want to hit the gym after filming?

334
00:09:52,940 --> 00:09:53,620
(So much energy)

335
00:09:54,040 --> 00:09:55,040
You're that committed?

336
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:56,480
You two should film another episode.

337
00:09:56,760 --> 00:09:57,160
What?

338
00:09:58,080 --> 00:09:59,200
So now I have to work out

339
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:00,840
with everyone watching?

340
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:03,560
You still do Pilates, Teng?

341
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:05,480
(Wait, what?)
You do Pilates?

342
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:07,400
(Surprised?)
My muscles are just too tight.

343
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:08,080
You know?

344
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:09,720
I wanted to loosen up,

345
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:11,680
so I gave Pilates a try.

346
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:13,080
You have to lie flat, right?

347
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:15,080
I couldn't even lie flat on the machine.

348
00:10:15,760 --> 00:10:17,040
(Stiff as a board)
My whole body went numb.

349
00:10:17,040 --> 00:10:18,520
And I'd already paid

350
00:10:18,520 --> 00:10:19,880
for who knows how many classes.

351
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:21,920
(Such dedication)
Did you finish them all?

352
00:10:21,920 --> 00:10:22,840
I went once.

353
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:23,700
(Maybe next time)

354
00:10:26,100 --> 00:10:28,020
(Even rat-doll playtime needs limits)

355
00:10:29,180 --> 00:10:31,380
(Peace and quiet)

356
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:34,300
(Hello there)

357
00:10:36,251 --> 00:10:37,337
Bai Jingting.

358
00:10:37,977 --> 00:10:41,188
♪Nights when I miss you♪
(Bro)

359
00:10:41,190 --> 00:10:45,382
♪I wish you were here beside me♪

360
00:10:45,500 --> 00:10:48,308
(Messing with it)

361
00:10:55,220 --> 00:10:58,220
(In his own little world)

362
00:11:00,220 --> 00:11:02,780
(So graceful)

363
00:11:05,325 --> 00:11:07,050
(Anyu, want an apple?)

364
00:11:08,160 --> 00:11:10,460
(Time for another pose)

365
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:18,740
(Sit nicely and pay attention)

366
00:11:19,140 --> 00:11:20,685
(Never forgets his buddy)

367
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:23,542
(Let me show you the splits)

368
00:11:34,900 --> 00:11:38,540
(Finding Anyu the perfect spot)

369
00:11:38,880 --> 00:11:41,560
(A taste of Bai's childhood)

370
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:42,400
Up next,

371
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:43,560
we're going to try...

372
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:44,520
(Quick answer!)
Fermented bean juice.

373
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:45,160
Fermented bean juice?

374
00:11:45,160 --> 00:11:45,960
Fermented bean juice.

375
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:46,800
(Interested)
Fermented bean juice?

376
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:48,280
(Here's an idea!)
Winner drinks three bowls.

377
00:11:48,560 --> 00:11:49,440
Three bowls for the winner.

378
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:50,520
(Reward or punishment?)
The last person gets the milk.

379
00:11:50,940 --> 00:11:51,460
(Now we're talking!)

380
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:52,520
(Discussion on hold)
Chinese hamburger.

381
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:53,520
(Still hung up on fermented bean juice)
Any fermented bean juice?

382
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:54,120
This afternoon.

383
00:11:54,120 --> 00:11:55,840
Bai highly recommended this.

384
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:56,480
Tell us

385
00:11:56,480 --> 00:11:57,720
what makes this Chinese hamburger
so good.

386
00:11:57,720 --> 00:11:58,960
(Bai's personal pick)
I used to eat this all the time

387
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:00,920
back when I was in school.

388
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:02,440
The shop opened when I was a kid,

389
00:12:02,440 --> 00:12:03,560
(All ears!)
and it's still there today.

390
00:12:03,880 --> 00:12:04,760
What's in it?

391
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:06,600
(Chef's curious)
It's flatbread stuffed with...

392
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:07,080
Pork head meat?

393
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:07,720
(Caught the key word)
Pork.

394
00:12:08,280 --> 00:12:09,560
Pork head meat is delicious.

395
00:12:09,560 --> 00:12:10,600
Since when

396
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:12,320
does it have pork head meat?

397
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:13,560
(That's what the chef said!)
Didn't he say pork head meat?

398
00:12:13,560 --> 00:12:14,000
(You misheard!)
Pork.

399
00:12:14,457 --> 00:12:15,100
(Oh, I see!)
Oh.

400
00:12:15,280 --> 00:12:16,800
What's the shop called?

401
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:18,120
Xiejie Chinese hamburger.

402
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:19,640
That's a street name around here, right?

403
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:20,160
Yeah.

404
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:20,720
Xiejie.

405
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:22,280
("Shoe street"?)
Is it full of shoe stores?

406
00:12:22,640 --> 00:12:23,880
(Wrong character)
It means a slanted street.

407
00:12:24,920 --> 00:12:25,720
Shoe Street?

408
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,520
I thought it was tied to your childhood.

409
00:12:27,520 --> 00:12:28,600
So it should be Shoe Street,

410
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:29,000
right?

411
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,700
(A shoe obsession since childhood?)

412
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:32,400
(Time to dig in)
Bring out the Chinese hamburgers.

413
00:12:32,400 --> 00:12:33,160
Everyone, give it a try.

414
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:34,240
It's bursting at the seams.

415
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:35,120
(Fully loaded)
This one's got everything.

416
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:37,160
Egg, meat, and sausage.

417
00:12:37,160 --> 00:12:38,280
(The gym buddies)
Let's share one.

418
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:39,120
(Gym buddies*2)
We'll share.

419
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:39,880
Yeah, let's share.

420
00:12:40,080 --> 00:12:41,280
It looks pretty good.

421
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:42,160
Have a taste of Tong's...

422
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:43,560
Tong's Baildhood.
[*A verbal slip]

423
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:45,360
Bai's childhood.

424
00:12:45,880 --> 00:12:46,800
Tong's childhood.

425
00:12:46,880 --> 00:12:47,880
Tong's childhood?

426
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:50,080
Tong's childhood?

427
00:12:50,400 --> 00:12:52,920
(Foodie mode activated)
Did you used to eat this with soup?

428
00:12:52,920 --> 00:12:53,800
(Still on about fermented bean juice)
Fermented bean juice.

429
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:54,160
No.

430
00:12:54,160 --> 00:12:54,560
You know, that...

431
00:12:54,560 --> 00:12:55,320
What's it called?

432
00:12:55,320 --> 00:12:55,760
Lamb soup?

433
00:12:55,760 --> 00:12:56,600
Or tofu puff soup.

434
00:12:56,600 --> 00:12:57,200
(Checking the filling)

435
00:12:57,200 --> 00:12:58,720
Is that rice in there?

436
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:00,520
And green peppers.

437
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:03,080
The freshly baked bread smells amazing.

438
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:04,400
Did you eat these growing up,

439
00:13:04,840 --> 00:13:05,200
Bai?

440
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:07,000
Did they have eggs
and sausage back then?

441
00:13:07,280 --> 00:13:08,520
I don't think they had this combo.

442
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:10,520
At least they didn't add spicy strips.

443
00:13:10,520 --> 00:13:12,280
They've still got some standards.

444
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:14,840
It's good.

445
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:15,720
Not bad.

446
00:13:16,594 --> 00:13:19,300
(A different kind of guest star)

447
00:13:19,300 --> 00:13:22,300
(Feast mode activated)

448
00:13:23,580 --> 00:13:26,388
(One giant bite)

449
00:13:42,060 --> 00:13:44,860
(80% of the burger left)

450
00:13:44,860 --> 00:13:48,740
(40% left)

451
00:13:48,740 --> 00:13:50,260
(10% left)

452
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:53,000
(There's another one)
Bing, there's one more.

453
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,000
(There's another one)
I'm good, thanks.

454
00:13:54,600 --> 00:13:55,400
When Huang Jingyu

455
00:13:55,680 --> 00:13:56,640
picked me up earlier,

456
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:57,560
(Wait, I did what?)
I knew I hadn't eaten enough.

457
00:13:59,920 --> 00:14:01,520
Everyone admits they're light,

458
00:14:01,520 --> 00:14:03,000
but nobody gives me credit
for my skills.

459
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:08,720
Yunrui can tell his friends

460
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:10,360
that he actually got to fly
on this show.

461
00:14:10,620 --> 00:14:12,200
(He's got a point)

462
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:13,200
(Literally airborne)
I really flew.

463
00:14:13,680 --> 00:14:15,400
(Now it makes sense)
So that's a flying guest star.

464
00:14:15,400 --> 00:14:16,560
A briefly flying guest star.

465
00:14:20,780 --> 00:14:22,460
(Natural High crew's catch-up time)

466
00:14:31,560 --> 00:14:33,000
(Curious)
Chengcheng, how much weight did you lose?

467
00:14:33,800 --> 00:14:34,640
(Thinking back)
Over 5kg.

468
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:35,680
How long did it take?

469
00:14:36,520 --> 00:14:37,360
I've just kept it off.

470
00:14:37,640 --> 00:14:38,760
(Impressed)
That takes real dedication.

471
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:40,240
I really went all out once.

472
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:40,880
(How far did you go?)

473
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:41,760
I decided

474
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:43,440
to bike to and from work every day.

475
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:44,600
I did it for a week.

476
00:14:44,600 --> 00:14:45,920
Then I weighed myself and only lost

477
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:47,160
1kg.

478
00:14:47,160 --> 00:14:47,760
(How much?)
How many kilos?

479
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:49,160
1kg.

480
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:51,560
(Big effort, tiny results)
I could sweat off more than that.

481
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:52,880
Do you down fermented bean juice

482
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:54,160
(Genuinely curious)
or sip it slowly?

483
00:14:54,520 --> 00:14:55,320
Savor it.

484
00:14:55,640 --> 00:14:56,480
Savor it?

485
00:14:56,680 --> 00:14:58,840
You have to soak
the fried dough rings in it.

486
00:14:58,840 --> 00:15:00,080
I just can't stomach
fermented bean juice.

487
00:15:00,780 --> 00:15:02,300
(Hasn't even tried it)

488
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:03,760
Have I told you this story?

489
00:15:03,760 --> 00:15:04,560
No.

490
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:06,760
(EP5 (Part 2))
Back when we did the Spring Festival Gala,

491
00:15:06,760 --> 00:15:08,480
sometimes we'd finish really late,

492
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:09,440
so we'd stay at the studio

493
00:15:09,440 --> 00:15:10,800
instead of going home.

494
00:15:10,800 --> 00:15:12,960
Then we'd wake up around noon
the next day

495
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:13,960
and order food delivery.

496
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:15,760
I was only wearing pajama pants.

497
00:15:15,760 --> 00:15:17,040
The delivery guy

498
00:15:17,040 --> 00:15:17,920
showed up and knocked on the door.

499
00:15:17,920 --> 00:15:19,080
So I opened it like this,

500
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:20,600
reached around from behind the door,

501
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:22,200
and when I reached for the food,
he grabbed my hand.

502
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:23,240
(Reenacting the scene)
He said, "Don't worry, Teng,"

503
00:15:23,240 --> 00:15:24,440
"I won't tell anyone."

504
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:27,840
The guy grabbed Teng's hand
and wouldn't let go.

505
00:15:28,200 --> 00:15:29,240
And Teng,

506
00:15:29,840 --> 00:15:31,400
being so good to his fans,

507
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:32,800
just went along with it.

508
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:37,600
Fine, just one look.

509
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:40,040
Just a quick peek.

510
00:15:40,640 --> 00:15:42,880
(That's going a bit far)
That's way too much for fan service.

511
00:15:45,400 --> 00:15:47,120
(One of a kind)
Does that even count as fan service?

512
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:49,360
What's "fan sa"?
[*Fan service]

513
00:15:49,560 --> 00:15:51,160
You can't just do it once.

514
00:15:51,160 --> 00:15:52,240
You have to do a whole bunch.

515
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:54,520
"Fan sha".
[*Acting foolish]

516
00:15:54,900 --> 00:15:55,540
(Go on...)

517
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:57,120
Suddenly, we're all acting foolish.

518
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:58,080
Acting foolish?

519
00:15:59,760 --> 00:16:01,760
Oh, that's the Northeastern saying
I know.

520
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:07,280
(Time for a real explanation)
No, it means things like...

521
00:16:07,760 --> 00:16:09,280
making a heart for your fans.

522
00:16:09,280 --> 00:16:10,280
That's "fan sa".
[*Fan service]

523
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:11,960
Then why call it "sa"? [*To scatter]

524
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:13,680
Like showering people with love?

525
00:16:13,680 --> 00:16:14,640
I think...

526
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:17,640
it comes straight from English.

527
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:18,080
I think so.

528
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:18,960
"Fan sha".
[*Acting foolish]

529
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:20,680
Something funny happened the other day.

530
00:16:20,680 --> 00:16:21,800
I was at a promotional event.

531
00:16:23,080 --> 00:16:24,960
A fan held up a sign asking
for fan service.

532
00:16:24,960 --> 00:16:25,600
I had no clue.

533
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:26,760
(Totally clueless)
I was stunned.

534
00:16:28,560 --> 00:16:29,360
It's English.

535
00:16:30,540 --> 00:16:31,600
Fan service.

536
00:16:32,240 --> 00:16:33,560
That's where "fan sa" comes from.
[*Fan service]

537
00:16:33,560 --> 00:16:34,760
So "serving your fans"?

538
00:16:35,394 --> 00:16:36,731
(You're right)

539
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:39,280
Then in Teng's case,

540
00:16:39,280 --> 00:16:40,760
he'd have to keep fanning that door.

541
00:16:42,120 --> 00:16:43,760
(Teng's Northeastern take)
It means doing something stupid.

542
00:16:44,400 --> 00:16:45,160
Acting like a fool.

543
00:16:45,320 --> 00:16:46,680
So what if a fan

544
00:16:46,680 --> 00:16:47,800
asked you

545
00:16:47,800 --> 00:16:48,360
for some fan service?

546
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:49,240
What would you do?

547
00:16:49,668 --> 00:16:50,902
(You little troublemaker)

548
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:56,960
Maybe that's what he meant.

549
00:16:57,760 --> 00:16:59,000
He told you not to worry.

550
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:00,200
He wouldn't tell anyone.

551
00:17:00,440 --> 00:17:01,360
But then he asked

552
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:02,360
if he could take just one peek.

553
00:17:05,240 --> 00:17:07,800
Let's say you've got a bag

554
00:17:07,800 --> 00:17:09,680
covered in photo cards

555
00:17:10,079 --> 00:17:12,400
or little plush toys.

556
00:17:13,040 --> 00:17:14,920
That's called an ita bag.

557
00:17:15,240 --> 00:17:16,160
Ita bag.

558
00:17:16,540 --> 00:17:17,260
(Learned something new)

559
00:17:17,820 --> 00:17:19,860
(A big fitness discussion)

560
00:17:20,119 --> 00:17:21,839
(Fitness talk)
Ever go ages without working out,

561
00:17:21,839 --> 00:17:24,359
then jump into something competitive

562
00:17:24,359 --> 00:17:26,400
and your heart rate shoots
through the roof?

563
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:28,000
You start seeing stars.

564
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:31,000
(Been there)
When that happens, I stop moving.

565
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:32,320
So you've reached the point where...

566
00:17:32,640 --> 00:17:33,840
I see stars the second I move.

567
00:17:33,840 --> 00:17:34,520
(Exercise safely)
That's why I avoid

568
00:17:35,080 --> 00:17:36,120
high-intensity workouts.

569
00:17:36,960 --> 00:17:38,520
(Same here)
Sometimes running makes my lips tingle.

570
00:17:38,760 --> 00:17:39,200
Right around here.

571
00:17:40,120 --> 00:17:41,040
I haven't worked out in ages.

572
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:43,520
I can't run either.

573
00:17:43,520 --> 00:17:44,800
Cardio's not my thing.

574
00:17:45,680 --> 00:17:47,880
But I always see videos of you
running outdoors.

575
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:51,400
(Footage from online)

576
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:52,240
I make myself do it.

577
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:53,560
But I alternate running and walking.

578
00:17:53,560 --> 00:17:54,880
(Going at his own pace)
I run for two minutes,

579
00:17:54,880 --> 00:17:55,520
walk for one,

580
00:17:55,520 --> 00:17:56,320
then run for two more.

581
00:17:56,800 --> 00:17:57,880
You have to give your body time

582
00:17:57,880 --> 00:17:59,480
to work up to it.

583
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:01,400
If you've been sitting around
for six months,

584
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:02,640
you can't just go all out.

585
00:18:03,080 --> 00:18:05,320
If you only do weights...

586
00:18:07,222 --> 00:18:08,120
(No)

587
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:09,240
The more you rely on machines,

588
00:18:09,600 --> 00:18:10,400
(Mr. Huang explains)
the more

589
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:12,680
your overall performance

590
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:13,720
can actually suffer.

591
00:18:13,800 --> 00:18:15,520
(Chiming in)
Weight training really drains you.

592
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:16,560
It's exhausting.

593
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:17,160
Right.

594
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:18,800
The more you lift weights,

595
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:20,560
the faster you get tired

596
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:20,960
when you

597
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:21,720
wrestle someone.

598
00:18:23,920 --> 00:18:24,880
Let's see if I can lift you.

599
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:25,720
Bing, you'll hurt your back like that.

600
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:26,120
You need to...

601
00:18:33,560 --> 00:18:33,960
Easy, Bing.

602
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:38,040
(One-on-one lesson begins)
Let me show you a trick.

603
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:39,080
(Mr. Huang's private lesson)
Don't lift like that.

604
00:18:39,080 --> 00:18:40,560
That puts all the strain right here.

605
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:41,640
When you grab someone,

606
00:18:41,640 --> 00:18:43,000
(Listening carefully)
pull them one step forward first.

607
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:43,600
Then step in here.

608
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:44,560
See? Pull them forward,

609
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:45,640
then step right in.

610
00:18:46,120 --> 00:18:46,600
Plant your foot here.

611
00:18:46,600 --> 00:18:47,600
Now their weight's over you.

612
00:18:47,600 --> 00:18:48,080
Step right here,

613
00:18:48,080 --> 00:18:49,520
(Takeoff)
and up they go.

614
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:51,800
Got it?

615
00:18:52,160 --> 00:18:54,080
If you bend over like this,

616
00:18:54,080 --> 00:18:55,320
all the weight goes on your back.

617
00:18:55,320 --> 00:18:56,100
(Key takeaway)
That's how you get hurt.

618
00:18:56,600 --> 00:18:57,080
Got it.

619
00:18:57,794 --> 00:18:59,660
(Scanning for a target...)

620
00:18:59,660 --> 00:19:01,588
(Staring innocently)

621
00:19:01,700 --> 00:19:02,700
(Huh?)

622
00:19:03,820 --> 00:19:04,857
(Up, up and away)

623
00:19:05,120 --> 00:19:07,200
(Fast learner)
Way easier, right?

624
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:08,680
Not even in the same league, right?

625
00:19:10,020 --> 00:19:11,840
(Demonstrating the difference)

626
00:19:11,840 --> 00:19:12,400
(My turn)
I want to fly too.

627
00:19:12,780 --> 00:19:14,114
(Wish granted)

628
00:19:15,540 --> 00:19:16,460
(Instant regret)

629
00:19:19,930 --> 00:19:22,220
(New skill unlocked)

630
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:25,000
(Stirring the pot)
He's insulting you.

631
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:29,000
No, I'm not.

632
00:19:29,720 --> 00:19:31,240
Bing elbowed me first.

633
00:19:31,240 --> 00:19:32,680
He went like this...

634
00:19:32,680 --> 00:19:33,840
He did this, then that.

635
00:19:37,020 --> 00:19:38,440
(Eager to try)

636
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:39,480
Let me try.

637
00:19:39,860 --> 00:19:40,580
(Already knows how to pose)

638
00:19:42,800 --> 00:19:43,280
Now what?

639
00:19:43,280 --> 00:19:44,760
Step in. Further in.

640
00:19:44,760 --> 00:19:45,280
Where does my foot go?

641
00:19:45,280 --> 00:19:46,240
(Mr. Huang steps in)
Further. Right here.

642
00:19:46,240 --> 00:19:46,800
Step here.

643
00:19:49,040 --> 00:19:50,120
Pull his arm down.

644
00:19:50,120 --> 00:19:50,800
Pull this arm.

645
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:51,760
Lift this one up.

646
00:19:51,760 --> 00:19:52,160
Hand goes here.

647
00:19:52,160 --> 00:19:52,960
Why do you look so awkward?

648
00:19:52,960 --> 00:19:53,520
(Another fast learner)
Get lower.

649
00:19:53,520 --> 00:19:54,600
Get down by my waist.

650
00:19:56,120 --> 00:19:57,120
Lower.

651
00:19:57,120 --> 00:19:58,880
(One hand on the left)
Lower your head.

652
00:19:58,880 --> 00:20:00,240
Tuck your head under his arm.

653
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:01,640
(One hand on the right)
Head up.

654
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:02,800
Look up.

655
00:20:10,340 --> 00:20:12,100
Forget it.

656
00:20:12,280 --> 00:20:13,880
Some things just aren't for everyone.

657
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:18,940
(Bonus round: Guess Who's Breathing)

658
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:20,960
Round Two. Hard mode.

659
00:20:21,080 --> 00:20:23,920
For the next five minutes,
any sound counts.

660
00:20:23,960 --> 00:20:26,000
Guess who made it,
and you switch places.

661
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:27,000
Chengcheng, you're up first.

662
00:20:31,737 --> 00:20:33,234
(What's that sound?)

663
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:40,520
(Ready)
Li Yunrui.

664
00:20:50,740 --> 00:20:51,300
(Quick switch)

665
00:20:51,300 --> 00:20:52,580
(Over there)

666
00:20:57,220 --> 00:20:58,580
(No, over here)

667
00:21:03,380 --> 00:21:04,742
(Who is it?)

668
00:21:05,320 --> 00:21:05,800
Who's that?

669
00:21:08,760 --> 00:21:09,560
Bing.

670
00:21:16,297 --> 00:21:17,780
(What's going on?)

671
00:21:18,297 --> 00:21:19,565
(Testing his knee reflex)

672
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:26,000
WeTV subscribers,

673
00:21:26,360 --> 00:21:27,040
please save me.

674
00:21:27,100 --> 00:21:28,000
(A helpless Gen Z kid)

675
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:29,200
Who else? Come on.

676
00:21:31,680 --> 00:21:32,240
Shen Teng.

677
00:21:35,960 --> 00:21:37,200
No hitting before your turn.

678
00:21:37,440 --> 00:21:38,400
(An idea strikes)
Why didn't you say that earlier?

679
00:21:39,280 --> 00:21:40,240
Too bad for you.

680
00:21:40,240 --> 00:21:41,040
Lin.

681
00:21:41,040 --> 00:21:41,540
(Plan worked)

682
00:21:41,540 --> 00:21:42,220
(Hehe)

683
00:21:42,220 --> 00:21:43,020
(Not laughing anymore)

684
00:21:45,360 --> 00:21:46,320
Are you testing my knee reflexes?

685
00:21:46,320 --> 00:21:47,800
Checking if I've got a fake leg?

686
00:21:50,680 --> 00:21:51,840
Come on, stop and go.

687
00:21:51,840 --> 00:21:52,640
Stop and go.

688
00:21:52,920 --> 00:21:53,720
Stop and go.

689
00:22:01,160 --> 00:22:01,960
Fan Chengcheng.

690
00:22:03,940 --> 00:22:05,760
(Hiss)

691
00:22:08,280 --> 00:22:09,080
Hu.

692
00:22:11,840 --> 00:22:12,380
(Cough)

693
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:13,520
Hu.

694
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:15,800
Correct.

695
00:22:16,280 --> 00:22:17,040
Wow, that was...

696
00:22:17,040 --> 00:22:18,240
That was spot-on.

697
00:22:18,240 --> 00:22:19,320
This is tough.

698
00:22:20,280 --> 00:22:21,200
I didn't recognize the sound,

699
00:22:21,200 --> 00:22:21,960
but I figured

700
00:22:22,240 --> 00:22:23,160
he'd just been called out.

701
00:22:24,160 --> 00:22:25,920
(He's cracked the code)
So he'd probably be next.

702
00:22:27,320 --> 00:22:28,560
You already figured it out.

703
00:22:28,560 --> 00:22:29,480
That's one strategy.

704
00:22:29,908 --> 00:22:30,900
(Noted)

705
00:22:32,580 --> 00:22:33,000
(Tsk)

706
00:22:33,000 --> 00:22:33,800
Bai!

707
00:22:34,925 --> 00:22:35,360
(Uh)

708
00:22:35,800 --> 00:22:36,480
Bai.

709
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:38,880
Bai.

710
00:22:39,740 --> 00:22:40,440
(Waiting to catch Bai)

711
00:22:40,440 --> 00:22:42,900
(Waiting to catch Bai)
So you'll get Bai eventually, right?

712
00:22:45,900 --> 00:22:46,760
(Putting the plan into action)
Here, take it.

713
00:22:47,560 --> 00:22:48,160
Go over there.

714
00:22:49,920 --> 00:22:51,080
Twenty seconds left.

715
00:22:51,080 --> 00:22:52,240
I didn't disguise my voice well enough.

716
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:55,440
Huang Jingyu.

717
00:22:56,857 --> 00:22:57,520
(Sniff)

718
00:22:57,520 --> 00:22:58,320
Huang Jingyu.

719
00:22:59,405 --> 00:23:00,020
(Cough)

720
00:23:03,440 --> 00:23:03,920
Bing.

721
00:23:03,980 --> 00:23:05,860
(Failed to charge up)

722
00:23:06,220 --> 00:23:07,120
(Caught off guard)

723
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:13,320
(He's figured it out)
So Huang Jingyu is the bait.

724
00:23:16,360 --> 00:23:17,520
Ten seconds left, Bing.

725
00:23:21,188 --> 00:23:21,740
(Game over)

726
00:23:23,760 --> 00:23:24,440
Fan Chengcheng.

727
00:23:30,800 --> 00:23:31,960
With that raspy voice of yours,

728
00:23:31,960 --> 00:23:33,640
why even try to imitate him?

729
00:23:34,160 --> 00:23:35,920
Some things just aren't for everyone.

730
00:23:39,120 --> 00:23:40,120
One second left.

731
00:23:40,120 --> 00:23:41,360
Chengcheng gets one last shot.

732
00:23:42,920 --> 00:23:44,440
Make sure he hasn't switched
to a metal bat.

733
00:23:46,520 --> 00:23:47,920
(Teasing Chengcheng)
Got a spiked club instead?

734
00:23:49,240 --> 00:23:50,040
Go.

735
00:24:07,840 --> 00:24:08,640
Bing.

736
00:24:09,020 --> 00:24:10,340
(Going full beatdown mode)

737
00:24:13,460 --> 00:24:14,060
(Panting)

738
00:24:14,400 --> 00:24:15,440
Is there a second round?

739
00:24:15,440 --> 00:24:16,240
Or a third?

740
00:24:17,680 --> 00:24:18,680
I don't even need to think.

741
00:24:18,680 --> 00:24:19,200
Where's Teng?

742
00:24:20,660 --> 00:24:21,280
(Still panting)

743
00:24:21,280 --> 00:24:22,560
That knocked the wind out of you, huh?
